Hi all,

the documentation of the LaTeX3 sources seems to be broken with the
latest TeXlive pretest. (pdf dating July 13, 2010)
All macro names in boxes are next to each other instead of being below
each other. That makes some things unreadable.
E.g. page 6 (page 19 in the pdf) contains the boxed line:

\GetIdInfo|\filename|\filenameext|\filedate|\fileversion|\filetimestamp|\=
fileauthor|\fi

the rest is out of the pdf page and thus unreadable.

Maybe there is a problem with the l3doc class?

It would be nice if this could be fixed as these boxes are quite
important to understand the documentation.

cheers
Arno


